<h3 id="research-question">Research question</h3>

<p>Can a large multimodal model compare clinical data from multiple time points and reason about progression, rather than interpreting one exam in isolation?</p>

<h3 id="what-the-benchmark-evaluates">What the benchmark evaluates</h3>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Temporal Perception QA:</strong> identifies changes between clinical time points.</li>
  <li><strong>Temporal Reasoning QA:</strong> uses changes across exams to answer questions about progression and related clinical context.</li>
</ul>

<p>The benchmark is derived from longitudinal chest X-rays in MIMIC-CXR. The evaluation found that the tested models struggled to ground their answers in evidence across time points; the paper reports results and error analyses by task.</p>

<p>The <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Chengfeng233/ELTLM-Bench">dataset repository</a> provides questions and reference answers. Access to the underlying images follows the <a href="https://physionet.org/content/mimic-cxr/2.1.0/">PhysioNet MIMIC-CXR access requirements</a>.</p>
